#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""aloud — BLAST survivors that were then spoken.

tacit classifies a call-site as TACIT (omitted), SHADOW (literal equal to
the default), OVERRIDE, or BOUND. A default-moving diff is a BLAST of
tacit riders plus FOSSIL restatements of the *old* literal.

That two-point picture cannot tell a BLAST survivor that later *said the
new default* from one that stayed omitted, and it cannot tell that
speaking from a SHADOW of the old value. Both later SHADOW-of-new sites
look the same at HEAD: one rode the blast silently and then pinned 0.45;
one already wrote 0.45 before the default moved (PRE).

aloud is the third snapshot. After a BLAST (OLD → NEW), look at LATER:

    MUTE    TACIT at NEW, still TACIT later — stayed omitted
    ALOUD   TACIT at NEW, later SHADOW of the *new* default
            (FOSSIL of the new value, not the old)
    FOSSIL  restates the *old* default
    PRE     already restated the new default at the BLAST
    LATE    not a survivor; later already SHADOW of the new default
            (the false ALOUD: born speaking, never rode the blast)
    FRESH   not a survivor; later TACIT
    LOCK    later some other literal
    BOUND   later a non-literal
    GONE    survivor disappeared

A site that was TACIT and later became an explicit restatement of the new
default is a different object than a site that stayed omitted, and
different from SHADOW-of-old.
"""
